    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "291b6dce_1a3ebc4d",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Caps.h",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 73,
      "author": {
        "id": 18914
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-20T15:30:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "While the set index is different in Vulkan for reading the dst from input vs. loading msaa from resolve(* see note for why), the loading MSAA SkSL is indeed custom-defined within backends \u0026 we can reference backend-specific static definitions of input attachment indices from pipelines at the time we need them from the command buffer. So we can in fact do that. Yay for conciseness!\n\nI actually went ahead and removed the definition `fInputAttachmentSetIdx` seeing as it can\u0027t be used yet (seeing as SkSL generation does not reference it and Vulkan does not yet have the concept of using input attachments for dst reading until las ter), so I imagine some compilers would complain.\n\n*Dst reads from the input attachment descriptors only need to be updated once per renderpass (less frequently than other descriptors), so having them earlier on in the container of sets is ideal such that changes to other descriptors or sets do not \"disturb\" this set and trigger the need to re-bind.",
      "parentUuid": "7dbed019_e825364d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 73,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "3639c997a09e5597806ff6be358808a92ab7fd7e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
